course: dictionary
lesson: 2739
title: Dirty: more than mud
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word dirty has more than one meaning. Its main meaning is not clean, covered with dirt, mud, dust or germs. «Wash dirty hands before you eat» tells you what to do: dirty means you need to wash.
explain: Dirty can also mean not fair or honest, as in «a dirty trick». Here the clue is the trick: someone is cheating, so dirty does not mean covered in mud. Ask yourself what word would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Dirty can be rude too. «He gave me a dirty look» means an angry look, not a look at mud. Dirty can also be a verb, meaning to make something dirty. Check the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: Dirty is an adjective: dirty, dirtier, dirtiest.
fact: «Dirty» means not clean, covered with dirt, mud, dust or germs.
fact: «Dirty» can mean not fair, as in «a dirty trick», which means cheating.
fact: «Smog» is a dirty haze of smoke and car fumes that builds up in still air.
fact: Dirty hands spread germs, so wash them before eating and after the toilet.
exercise: «Wash dirty hands before eating and after the toilet.» What does dirty mean here? | *Not clean, covered in dirt or germs | Very old | Happy and full of fun | Wet with rain
exercise: Ellie says, «That was a dirty trick.» What does dirty suggest? | Clean and shiny | Kind and generous | *Not fair, like cheating | Very hungry
exercise: What is the opposite of dirty? | Smoky | *Clean | Rude | Muddy
test: «He gave me a dirty look.» What does dirty look mean? | A look at a muddy field | A look that is very clean | *An angry or unkind look | A tired yawn
test: Sam says dirty can be a verb. «The children dirtied their shoes in the mud.» What does dirtied mean? | Put away | *Made dirty | Dried out | Cleaned up
exam: «Never walk in floodwater, which can be fast, dirty and electrified.» What does dirty mean in this sentence? | Rude or unkind | Dry and warm | *Not clean, full of dirt and germs | Not fair or honest
